{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  BUNDLE20 FLASH
  snippets/bundle20-flash.liquid
  ============================================================

  The red BUNDLE20 discount line. Single source of truth, used in
  two places:

    snippets/product-details.liquid   PDP, sits under the black price
    snippets/product-item.liquid      collection card, under the price

  PDP keeps the red bullet. Cards do not.

  Current wording:
    PDP    Save £161.40 extra with code BUNDLE20
    Card   Save £161.40 extra with BUNDLE20

  The card drops "code" to save space in the two-across mobile grid.

  The saving is 20% of the CURRENT SELLING PRICE, not of the compare-at
  price. On a bundle already reduced from £896.88 to £806.99, the line
  reads £161.40 (20% of 806.99), which is the extra the code takes off
  on top of the existing reduction. That matches how Shopify applies a
  percentage discount, so the number a customer sees at checkout is the
  number shown here.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
  HOW ELIGIBILITY IS DECIDED

  PDP and card both check the PRODUCT'S OWN collections against
  b20_collection_handles below. Same rule in both places, so a bundle
  card carries the flash wherever it appears: its bundle collection,
  Shop All, search, homepage tiles, related products.

  This replaced an earlier version where the card checked which
  collection PAGE the shopper was on. That was cheaper to render but it
  silently hid the flash on any collection not in the list. Hex Dumbbell
  Bundles (hex-dumbbell-bundles) was the example: its products sit in
  packages-sets and home-dumbbell-sets so the discount applied fine, but
  the cards said nothing about it.

  Cost of the current approach: product.collections is one lookup per
  card, so 24 to 48 per collection page render. Collection pages are
  served from Shopify's full page cache for anonymous traffic, so most
  visitors never pay it. Cache misses do.

  IF COLLECTION PAGE SPEED BECOMES A PROBLEM, stop using collections for
  this and put a 'bundle20' tag on the products instead. product.tags is
  already loaded with the product in a card loop, so it costs nothing.
  The eligibility check below becomes a single tags test rather than a
  loop. That also decouples the theme from collection structure
  entirely. It needs the products tagging in admin first.
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  CONFIG. This block is the only thing you need to touch.

  b20_enabled = false  turns the whole feature off everywhere,
  PDP and collection cards, instantly. Save the file and it is gone.
  No other file needs changing.

  b20_percent must match the actual discount set up in Shopify
  Discounts. If it changes from 20%, change it here too or the site
  will quote the wrong number.

  b20_show_on_sale_items = true means bundles that already have a
  compare-at price still get the flash. Set false to go back to hiding
  it on anything already reduced.

  ---- WORDING ----

  [amount] is replaced with the cash saving. Use square brackets, not
  curly ones: a curly brace inside a Liquid string breaks the parser.

  PDP and card are separate on purpose so the card can be shortened for
  mobile without touching the PDP.

  Keep APOSTROPHES OUT of the PDP label: it is dropped into a
  JavaScript string and an apostrophe will break it.

  b20_card_label_range is used on cards showing a "From £x" price. A
  cash figure there would have to be based on the cheapest variant, so
  it would understate the saving on every other variant.

  Shorter card options if mobile is still tight:
    'Extra 20% with BUNDLE20'
    '[amount] off with BUNDLE20'

  ---- COLLECTIONS ----

  b20_collection_handles is the list that decides eligibility. It is
  deliberately identical to the collections the BUNDLE20 discount itself
  targets in Shopify Discounts, checked 10/09/26.

  DO NOT add a collection here that is not on the discount. The site
  would promise a saving that does not apply at checkout. Add it to the
  discount first, then here.

  b20_pdp_gap_below is the space between the flash and the USP strip
  (In Stock / Express Delivery / Lift Now Pay Later) underneath it.
  ------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign b20_enabled            = false -%}
{%- assign b20_percent            = 20 -%}
{%- assign b20_show_on_pdp        = true -%}
{%- assign b20_show_on_cards      = true -%}
{%- assign b20_show_on_sale_items = true -%}
{%- assign b20_pdp_gap_below      = '20px' -%}

{%- assign b20_pdp_label        = 'Save [amount] extra with code BUNDLE20' -%}
{%- assign b20_card_label       = 'Save [amount] extra with BUNDLE20' -%}
{%- assign b20_card_label_range = 'Save 20% extra with BUNDLE20' -%}

{%- assign b20_collection_handles = 'packages-sets,home-dumbbell-sets,yoga-pilates-bundles,kettlebell-bundles,barbell-bundles,conditioning-bundles' -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- end of config, logic below ---------- {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Expected params:
    b20_context   'pdp' or 'card'
    b20_product   the product object
    b20_price     selling price in cents to base the maths on
    b20_on_sale   true if the product already has a compare-at price
    b20_is_range  card only, true when the card shows a 'From' price
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign b20_render     = false -%}
{%- assign b20_price_ok   = false -%}
{%- assign b20_context_ok = false -%}

{%- if b20_price > 0 -%}
  {%- if b20_show_on_sale_items or b20_on_sale != true -%}
    {%- assign b20_price_ok = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if b20_context == 'pdp' and b20_show_on_pdp -%}
  {%- assign b20_context_ok = true -%}
{%- elsif b20_context == 'card' and b20_show_on_cards -%}
  {%- assign b20_context_ok = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if b20_enabled and b20_price_ok and b20_context_ok -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    One rule for both contexts. Breaks on the first match, so a product
    sitting in several bundle collections costs the same as one sitting
    in a single collection.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign b20_handles = b20_collection_handles | split: ',' -%}

  {%- for b20_coll in b20_product.collections -%}
    {%- if b20_handles contains b20_coll.handle -%}
      {%- assign b20_render = true -%}
      {%- break -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

{%- endif -%}

{%- if b20_render -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Prices are in cents. Round after applying the multiplier so we never
    render a fraction of a penny. 20% of 80699 = 16139.8, rounds to
    16140, renders as £161.40.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign b20_pct_dec = b20_percent | divided_by: 100.0 -%}
  {%- assign b20_saving  = b20_price | times: b20_pct_dec | round -%}
  {%- assign b20_money   = b20_saving | money -%}

  {%- if b20_context == 'pdp' -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The label is split on [amount] so the two halves can wrap around the
      live figure in x-text. Anything before [amount] becomes the prefix,
      anything after becomes the suffix, so the wording stays editable in
      one place at the top of this file.

      x-text keeps the saving in step with variant switching, and reads
      selectedVariant.price, which is the SELLING price, so a bundle with
      a compare-at price gets 20% of what it is actually sold for. No
      range problem here because a variant is always selected.

      It deliberately ignores the PDP add-on total (Arm Blaster etc):
      BUNDLE20 is scoped to the bundle collections only, so an add-on is
      not discounted and folding it in would overstate the saving. Do not
      wire this to the product:addons:totals event. That event drives the
      main price above, and the two numbers are correctly different.

      Falls back to the Liquid figure before Alpine boots, so there is no
      flash of an empty or wrong value.

      Base class kept as .bogohp-flash on purpose. Renaming risks losing
      an override sitting in custom.css (178KB, not grepped yet). The
      spacing lives on a --pdp modifier rather than the base class so it
      cannot leak into anything else already using .bogohp-flash.
    {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- assign b20_parts = b20_pdp_label | split: '[amount]' -%}
    {%- assign b20_pre  = b20_parts[0] -%}
    {%- assign b20_post = b20_parts[1] | default: '' -%}
    {%- assign b20_pdp_text = b20_pdp_label | replace: '[amount]', b20_money -%}

    <div class="bogohp-flash bogohp-flash--pdp">
      <span class="bogohp-flash__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span
        class="bogohp-flash__text"
        x-text="'{{ b20_pre }}' + formatPrice(Math.round((selectedVariant &amp;&amp; selectedVariant.price ? selectedVariant.price : {{ b20_price }}) * {{ b20_pct_dec }})) + '{{ b20_post }}'"
      >{{ b20_pdp_text }}</span>
    </div>
    <style>
      .bogohp-flash {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 9px;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        width: fit-content;
        max-width: 100%;
        color: #BE0707;
        font-family: 'Roboto Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
        font-size: 14px;
        font-weight: 500;
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
        line-height: 1.3;
      }
      .bogohp-flash__dot {
        width: 8px;
        height: 8px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: #BE0707;
        flex: 0 0 auto;
      }
      .bogohp-flash--pdp {
        margin-bottom: {{ b20_pdp_gap_below }};
      }
    </style>

  {%- else -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Utility classes only, no <style> tag. This snippet renders once per
      card, so an inline style block here would repeat 24 to 48 times per
      collection page for no benefit. text-red is the theme class already
      used for the strikethrough 'was' price.

      No Alpine here. Cards have no variant switcher, so a static Liquid
      figure is correct and costs nothing at runtime.

      text-balance spreads the wrap evenly across lines rather than
      orphaning a single word, which is what makes a three line label
      look worst in a two-across mobile grid.
    {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- if b20_is_range -%}
      {%- assign b20_card_text = b20_card_label_range -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign b20_card_text = b20_card_label | replace: '[amount]', b20_money -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <p class="bundle20-card-flash text-red text-xs font-normal leading-tight text-balance">{{ b20_card_text }}</p>

  {%- endif -%}

{%- endif -%}
